# Mobile UI (iOS and Android)

UI only. Logic, providers, models, l10n, and tokens stay in root `lib/`. Details: `apps/reader_flutter/lib/mobile/CLAUDE.md`.

## Where widgets live

- New screens and widgets go in `lib/mobile/` (`screens/`, `widgets/catalog/`, `widgets/shell/`, `widgets/reader/`).
- `lib/widgets/` is legacy. `liquid_glass_nav_bar.dart` there re-exports `lib/mobile/widgets/shell/`. When you edit another legacy widget, move it into `lib/mobile/`.
- Copy `lib/mobile/screens/mobile_home_screen.dart` for a new mobile screen.

## Conventions

- Touch-first: `Scaffold`, `SafeArea`, `RefreshIndicator`, bottom nav. Sidebars, hover cards, and web grids belong on web and desktop.
- Shell tabs: Home, Purchases (only when the user has a purchase), Profile, plus Admin when `user.canManageBooks`. Settings maps to Profile.
- Pad scroll content by `LiquidGlassNavBar.bottomInset` (`extendBody: true`).
- Tokens come from `lib/design/` (`AppColors`, `AppSpace`, `AppRadius`).
- Strings via `AppLocalizations.of(context)`.
- Covers use `BookCoverPoster` with a stable index into the full list. One `AppGreetingCard` per shell screen.
- Touch targets are at least 48dp. Lists use `BouncingScrollPhysics`.

```dart
import '../../providers/catalog_providers.dart';
import '../../design/app_tokens.dart';
```

Run: `make reader-run-android`, `make reader-run-ios`.
